  "style": {
    "id": "cyanotype",
    "name": "Cyanotype",
    "description": "Sunlight makes the print: a sheet of pale yellow-green sensitised paper pinned to a light wooden board in strong sun, with a fern frond, a brass key, a grey-blue feather and a strip of lace lying on it as flat procedural objects with real thickness and shadows. Every uncovered point collects a dose (the closed-form integral of the sun over the time it was uncovered); the paper darkens to bronze-grey around the objects, the feather lifted early prints as a half-dark ghost, the others leave crisp pale silhouettes. The sheet slides into a white enamel tray, a wave of water crosses it and the exposed paper floods to deep Prussian blue with paper-white shapes. One shader on the sheet looks colour up from (dose, washed). Soft thuds, a warm pad that brightens with the sun, lift whooshes, a water slosh and a rising chime.",
